ORDER: forward

PART 1: WHAT A ROW IS
   (1a) RZ /(?<k>\d)(?:;(?<h>\d))*/, 1110 subjects: `(h: <5)` read over the match row (every pass, LEFT JOIN) vs over pass rows (some pass): differ 500 (smallest '0;0;5': FAILS / HOLDS)
        LST /(?:(?<h>\d)(?::(?<m>\d))?,)*/, 43 lists: `((h, m): m < h)` match row vs pass rows: differ 10 (smallest '1,6:2,': FAILS / HOLDS)
   (1b) zero passes on RZ `3` (k = 3, no h): `(h: <5, k: 3..7)` FAILS, `(h?: <5, k: 3..7)` HOLDS (M1) / HOLDS (M2c), `some((h: <5))` FAILS; on `9`: `(h?: <5, k: 3..7)` FAILS (the outside k still tested: zero-pass-record)
   (1c) T2 /(?<h>\d{1,2})(?::(?<m>\d\d))?/, 11110 subjects, q := t2 & ((h, m): late), late = padded(>= (9, 30)):
        `t2 & !q` per whole subject (S1) holds on 1970; per span (S2, searched) on 11110; `!` of the searched q on 1970; NOT ((h, m): late) whole 1878, searched 11106
        S1 vs S2 complement                          differ  9140 (smallest '9:30')
        S2 complement vs complement of searched q    differ  9140 (smallest '9:30')

PART 2: THE TWO NOTS (and the complement on the set), unmarked and marked
